# Fixed defect 2692, 2026-11-22, lane-crossing, a shape beside it: `==` on
# another module's record holding a `partial` record, whose fields this
# program cannot all see. Symptom: accepted, where the same records declared
# in the one module, before the comparison, were refused. Cause: the walk
# asking whether a type reaches a `partial` record read the fields' lowered
# types, and the record's fields were lowered only once the declarations'
# walk reached its module, after the root's `same` (spec § 13).
use stats

function same(a: stats.Sized, b: stats.Sized) -> bool
    return a == b  #~ ffi_partial_operation

function main()
    print(same(a: stats.made(), b: stats.made()))
